This page is a documentation starter. Replace it with one workflow that matters to your users.

## 1. Define one outcome

A useful guide begins with a result. This starter adds a small JSON status endpoint.

```go
func ProductStatus(w http.ResponseWriter, _ *http.Request) {
	w.Header().Set("Content-Type", "application/json")
	_ = json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(map[string]string{
		"status": "ready",
	})
}
```

## 2. Register the route

Keep the route close to the rest of the HTTP surface:

```go
mux.HandleFunc("GET /product-status", ProductStatus)
```

## 3. Verify the result

```bash
curl http://localhost:8090/product-status
```

```json
{
  "status": "ready"
}
```

